.TH PSF-PHP2SHELL-EDGE-TEST 8 "30 October 2026" "psf-security-patches 26.10.30-1.0.0" "System Administration"
.ad l
.SH NAME
.ad l
psf-php2shell-edge-test \- Usage:
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ad l
.B /\:\:opt/\:\:psf\-security\-patches/\:\:php/\:\:edge/\:\:php2shell\-edge\-test.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.ad l
.PP
\&./php2shell\-edge\-test.sh [options] URL
.RS 2
.nf
\-\-expect MODE    block     (default) the guard is enforcing: a multipart
                           POST to URL must get 403
                 dry-run   the .htaccess dry run: a multipart POST must NOT
                           get 403 and must carry
                             X-PHP2Shell-Guard
                 log-only  the .conf or nginx log-only mode: a
                   multipart
                           POST must NOT get 403 (add \-\-log FILE
                             to also
                           confirm the guard logged it)
\-\-allow PATH     a path on your allowlist (for example /wp\-admin/async\-
                 upload.php). A multipart POST to it must NOT get
                   403, and
                 one to PATH.bak must get 403 when enforcing
\-\-log FILE       a log the guard writes to; used with \-\-expect log-only
\-\-host NAME      send this Host header (the URL may be 127.0.0.1)
\-\-insecure       do not verify a TLS certificate
\-h, \-\-help, version
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.ad l
.TP
\fB/\:\:opt/\:\:psf\-security\-patches/\:\:php/\:\:edge/\:\:php2shell\-edge\-test.sh\fR
.ad l
The script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.ad l
psf\-security\-patches(7).
